// ============================================================================
// Resolution · CAST & INSTANCEOF-PATTERN EXACT-TYPING
//
// `((FooImpl) x).bar()` and `if (o instanceof FooImpl f) f.bar()` are the programmer
// *asserting* a concrete type. expr-type.dl already NARROWS the receiver to that type
// (cast_type_resolves / pattern_var_type). This layer adds the missing piece: mark such
// a receiver EXACT so the CHA subtype-fan is suppressed (via callee-resolution.dl's
// existing !call_exact_receiver gate), the same way a monomorphic local / direct `new`
// is treated. In Java a variable can't be *used* at a narrowed type without a cast or a
// pattern binding, so these two cases ARE "instanceof narrowing" — there is no separate
// bare-instanceof receiver to handle.
//
// EXACT only when the asserted type is a CONCRETE class (CLASS_TYPE, non-abstract):
//   - FINAL concrete class  -> fully sound (no subtypes exist).
//   - non-final concrete    -> a strong type assertion; treated exact (accuracy-first:
//                              a subtype override could in principle differ = small FN risk,
//                              acceptable per the accuracy-over-completeness policy).
//   - INTERFACE / ABSTRACT   -> NOT exact: casting to an interface/abstract type pins no
//                              single impl, so the fan is still needed and correct.
//
// STRATIFICATION: LOW. cast_type_resolves / instanceof_type_resolves / pattern_var_type
// are type-reference resolutions (no expr_call_candidate dep); concrete_class_type is a
// base-fact lookup. So feeding the negated exact gate stays stratified, like the existing
// monomorphic-local rule.
//
// java_type (14): 3 typeCategory  5 typeModifier  13 hash
// java_expression (25): 0 kind 1 edgeRole 10 literalValue(name) 24 uniqueHash
// cast_type_resolves (4): 0 prov 1 expr 2 ref 3 type
// ============================================================================

// A concrete, instantiable class type: CLASS_TYPE and not abstract (its runtime type is
// itself modulo rare subclasses; final ⇒ exactly itself).
concrete_class_type(t) :- java_type(_, _, _, "CLASS_TYPE", _, mod, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, t),
    !match(".*ABSTRACT_MODIFIER.*", mod).

// (Foo) x — cast to a concrete class ⇒ EXACT receiver (suppress the subtype fan).
expr_exact_type(e, t) :- java_expression("CAST_EXPRESSION", _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, e),
    cast_type_resolves(_, e, _, t),
    concrete_class_type(t).

// if (o instanceof Foo f) f.m() — pattern-variable use of a concrete class ⇒ EXACT receiver.
expr_exact_type(e, t) :- java_expression("IDENTIFIER_REFERENCE", _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, name, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, e),
    name != "",
    expr_ultimate_method("client", e, method),
    pattern_var_type(name, method, _, t),
    concrete_class_type(t).
